    "created_at": "2025-04-28T12:10:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-28T12:10:23Z",
    "body": "I see, I think I got confused by this comment from @simon-friedberger: https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1655#issuecomment-1943496127. That suggested \"redirect-like\" behavior would also count.\n\nDid someone analyze whether an attacker could use HTTP-redirect loop detection as some kind of side channel?\n\nI understand why we'd want to bail out early for an end-user-facing feature so modulo the attacker concern it makes sense to me to define the HTTP-redirect loop detection and use it for HTTPS upgrades. It seems we could build this on top of request's URL list concept?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
